{"id":14259,"artist":"Henry Alford, George J. Elvey","title":"Come, Ye Thankful People Come","lyrics_plain":"Come, ye thankful people, come,\nRaise the song of harvest home!\nAll is safely gathered in,\nEre the winter storms begin.\nGod our Maker doth provide\nFor our wants to be supplied;\nCome to God's own temple, come,\nRaise the song of harvest home.\nAll the world is God's own field,\nFruit as praise to God we yield;\nWheat and tares together sown\nAre to joy or sorrow grown;\nFirst the blade and then the ear,\nThen the full corn shall appear;\nLord of harvest, grant that we\nWholesome grain and pure may be.\nFor the Lord our God shall come,\nAnd shall take the harvest home;\nFrom the field shall in that day\nAll offenses purge away,\nGiving angels charge at last\nIn the fire the tares to cast;\nBut the fruitful ears to store\nIn the garner evermore.\nEven so, Lord, quickly come,\nBring Thy final harvest home;\nGather Thou Thy people in,\nFree from sorrow, free from sin,\nThere, forever purified,\nIn Thy presence to abide;\nCome, with all thine angels, come,\nRaise the glorious harvest home.\nAmen.","lyrics_synced":"[00:00.00] Come, ye thankful people, come,\n[00:04.80] Raise the song of harvest home!\n[00:09.60] All is safely gathered in,\n[00:14.40] Ere the winter storms begin.\n[00:19.20] God our Maker doth provide\n[00:24.00] For our wants to be supplied;\n[00:28.80] Come to God's own temple, come,\n[00:33.60] Raise the song of harvest home.\n[00:38.39] All the world is God's own field,\n[00:42.75] Fruit as praise to God we yield;\n[00:47.12] Wheat and tares together sown\n[00:51.48] Are to joy or sorrow grown;\n[00:55.84] First the blade and then the ear,\n[01:00.21] Then the full corn shall appear;\n[01:04.57] Lord of harvest, grant that we\n[01:08.93] Wholesome grain and pure may be.\n[01:13.30] For the Lord our God shall come,\n[01:17.66] And shall take the harvest home;\n[01:22.03] From the field shall in that day\n[01:26.39] All offenses purge away,\n